jobs.description:
At Globus Medical, we move with a sense of urgency to deliver innovations that improve the quality of life of patients with musculoskeletal disorders. Our team is inspired by the needs of these patients, and the surgeons and healthcare providers who treat them. We embrace a culture of exceptional response by partnering with researchers and educators to transform clinical insights into tangible solutions. Our solutions improve the techniques and outcomes of surgery so patients can resume their lives as quickly as possible.
Position Summary:
The Senior Software Engineer will be responsible for major software modules for Robotics products.

Essential Functions:

- Develop prototypes, proofs of concept in addition to production-quality solutions;

- Ensure efficient performance and scalability of solutions;

- Contribute to design, testing and documentation of software solutions;

- Provide technical support to manufacturing, internal testing, and external customers as necessary; and

- Ensure compliance with applicable governmental laws, rules, and regulations, both in the United States and internationally, by completing introductory and annual training and maintaining knowledge of compliance as it applies to the role.
Standard company benefits.

- 

Qualifications:

- Requires a Bachelor’s degree or foreign equivalent in Information Technology, Computer Science, Computer Graphics, or a related field;

- 3 years of experience as a Software Engineer, Graphics Engineer, or in a related occupation;

- Experience working with Surgical navigation technologies, Image Registration, Image Processing, or Robotics;

- Experience with object-oriented analysis and design, multi-threading, and the Windows OS;

- Experience with software architecture and software development processes, including source control;

- Experience engineering high-performance CAD algorithms for a web-based platform;

- Experience building and maintaining CAD software components using C++ compiled to WebAssembly for browser-based deployment;

- Experience developing supporting tools and workflow components using JavaScript/TypeScript and Blender’s Python API;

- Experience supporting development of scalable 3D/CAD systems;

- Experience managing acquisition and preparation of high-quality technical data to improve application performance and algorithm reliability;

- Experience improving software performance by optimizing core modules, reducing CPU usage, and streamlining legacy code;

- Experience building data storage, point-cloud processing, and mesh-analysis tools;

- Experience engineering Unity plugins to support inter-language communication and automated testing workflows;

- Experience with Agile coordination and Scrum-based delivery support;

- Experience designing APIs, data models, sequence diagrams, and class diagrams; and

- Experience using JavaScript/TypeScript, Python, C#, GLSL, Unity, HLSL, Agile methodology, modern IDEs, Version Control Systems, QT Framework, Git, Jira, and Confluence.
#LI-DNI
Our Values :
Our Life Moves Us philosophy is built on four values: Passionate About Innovation, Customer Focused, Teamwork, and Driven.

- Passionate about Innovation : Improving patient care by delivering advanced technology to our customers is at the core of what we do. We are passionate in our role in improving the lives of patients by continuously developing better solutions.

- Customer Focused : We listen to our customers’ needs and respond with a sense of urgency.

- Teamwork : Working together, anything is possible. We value every person on our team and treat each other with respect. We are accountable to one another and support each other. Together, we make each other stronger.

- Driven : We pursue our mission with energy and passion. We are nimble, results-oriented and decisive. We overcome obstacles that arise in our quest to deliver solutions that will improve the lives of our customers and patients.

Equal Employment Opportunity :
Globus Medical is an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, age, disability, marital status, pregnancy, national origin or citizenship. We are committed to a diverse workforce. We value all employees’ talents and support an environment that is inclusive and respectful.

Other Duties :
Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice.
